    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-17T04:10:55+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-17T04:10:55+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-16T17:40:55Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-16T17:40:55Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred south of Western Australia, extends a ridge of high pressure over most of South Australia. The high and ridge will move slowly eastwards during the week to be in the Tasman Sea on Thursday. A low pressure system and associated trough over Western Australia will move over South Australia mid to late in the week.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-17T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-18T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-16T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-17T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers west of Coober Pedy, most likely from late this morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. A thunderstorm likely west of Coober Pedy, possibly severe with heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding. Winds east to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending north to northeasterly in the middle of the day then tending east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures around 30.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 5:20pm, UV Index predicted to reach 12 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-18T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-19T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-17T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-18T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of showers west of Coober Pedy, medium chance elsewhere. A thunderstorm likely. Thunderstorms possibly severe with destructive winds, giant hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending north to northeasterly 25 to 40 km/h during the morning then decreasing to 20 to 30 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 17 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching 26 to 34.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-19T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-18T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers east of Coober Pedy, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding east of Stuart Highway. Winds north to northwesterly 20 to 30 km/h increasing to 25 to 35 km/h during the morning then shifting south to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 17 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching 30 to 35.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the day then tending southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching 31 to 36.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
